hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18103","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, from Abu Las al-Khuzai who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mounted us on camels from the charity camels for the pilgrimage, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, we do not think these will carry us. He said: There is no camel of ours except that upon its hump is a devil, so mention the name of Allah over them when you ride them as I have commanded you, then use them fully for yourselves, for it is Allah, Mighty and Majestic, who carries."
"18104","Yaqoub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, and he was trustworthy, from Abu Las al-Khuzai who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mounted us on weak camels from the charity camels to the pilgrimage. He said: So we said to him: O Messenger of Allah, these camels are weak, we fear they will not carry us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no camel except that upon its hump is a devil, so ride them and mention the name of Allah over them as you have been commanded, then use them fully for yourselves, for it is Allah, Mighty and Majestic, who carries."
